# Game Code Benchmark Practice Brief

## System: Testable 3D Movement with Collision Response

### Core Pattern
```csharp
// Unity example - Godot equivalent uses KinematicBody.move_and_slide()
public class MovableEntity : MonoBehaviour
{
    [SerializeField] private float speed = 5f;
    [SerializeField] private float jumpForce = 10f;

    private CharacterController controller;
    private Vector3 velocity;
    private bool isGrounded;

    void Awake() => controller = GetComponent<CharacterController>();

    void Update()
    {
        HandleInput();
        ApplyGravity();
        HandleCollision();
        controller.Move(velocity * Time.deltaTime);
    }

    private void HandleInput()
    {
        var input = new Vector3(Input.GetAxis("Horizontal"), 0, Input.GetAxis("Vertical"));
        transform.Translate(input * speed * Time.deltaTime, Space.World);

        if (Input.GetButtonDown("Jump") && isGrounded)
            velocity.y = jumpForce;
    }

    private void ApplyGravity() => velocity.y += Physics.gravity.y * Time.deltaTime;
    private void HandleCollision()
    {
        isGrounded = controller.isGrounded;
        if (isGrounded && velocity.y < 0) velocity.y = -2f; // Ground stick
    }
}
```

---

## Executable Checklist

### ✅ **Movement System**
- [ ] Cap movement speed using `Vector3.ClampMagnitude()` 
- [ ] Use `CharacterController.isGrounded` or raycast down for ground detection
- [ ] Implement gravity accumulation, not frame-perfect application
- [ ] Separate input handling from physics response

### ✅ **Collision Response**
- [ ] Raycast/sweep before movement, don't just react after penetration
- [ ] Slide along collision normals using `.hit.normal`
- [ ] Store last movement direction for wall-jump recovery
- [ ] Zero velocity component into surfaces

### ✅ **State Machine (Minimal FSM)**
```csharp
enum EntityState { Idle, Moving, Jumping, Falling, Hurt }
EntityState currentState;

void TransitionTo(EntityState newState)
{
    ExitState(currentState);
    currentState = newState;
    EnterState(newState);
}
```

### ✅ **Pathfinding Boundary**
- [ ] A* operates on grid cells, not world positions directly
- [ ] Node cost = 1 ground, 3 wall, custom terrain types
- [ ] Diagonal = √2 penalty, not bonus
- [ ] Reach target node, then snap to exact position

### ✅ **ECS Boundary Rules**
- [ ] Systems read/write specific component arrays only
- [ ] Entities = ID + component array indices
- [ ] No FindObjectOfType in Update loops
- [ ] Archetype-based iteration for cache efficiency

